ption":"A sudden climb without a matching CPU rise usually means lock contention or interrupt storms.","fieldConfig":{"defaults":{"custom":{"drawStyle":"line","fillOpacity":10,"lineWidth":1,"showPoints":"never"},"unit":"short"},"overrides":[]},"gridPos":{"h":8,"w":12,"x":12,"y":10},"options":{"legend":{"displayMode":"list","placement":"bottom"},"tooltip":{"mode":"multi"}},"targets":[{"expr":"rate(node_context_switches_total[5m])","legendFormat":"context switches/s","refId":"A"},{"expr":"rate(node_intr_total[5m])","legendFormat":"interrupts/s","refId":"B"}],"title":"Context switches \u0026 interrupts","type":"timeseries"},{"collapsed":false,"gridPos":{"h":1,"w":24,"x":0,"y":18},"panels":[],"title":"Memory \u0026 pressure (RAM stress)","type":"row"},{"datasource":{"type":"prometheus","uid":"prometheus"},"fieldConfig":{"defaults":{"custom":{"drawStyle":"line","fillOpacity":10,"lineWidth":1,"showPoints":"never"},"min":0,"unit":"bytes"},"overrides":[{"matcher":{"id":"byName","options":"total"},"properties":[{"id":"custom.lineStyle","value":{"dash":[8,6],"fill":"dash"}},{"id":"custom.fillOpacity","value":0}]}]},"gridPos":{"h":8,"w":12,"x":0,"y":19},"options":{"legend":{"calcs":["lastNotNull","max"],"displayMode":"table","placement":"right"},"tooltip":{"mode":"multi","sort":"desc"}},"targets":[{"expr":"node_memory_MemTotal_bytes - node_memory_MemAvailable_bytes","legendFormat":"used (excl. reclaimable)","refId":"A"},{"expr":"node_memory_Cached_bytes","legendFormat":"cached","refId":"B"},{"expr":"node_memory_Buffers_bytes","legendFormat":"buffers","refId":"C"},{"expr":"node_memory_MemAvailable_bytes","legendFormat":"available","refId":"D"},{"expr":"node_memory_MemTotal_bytes","legendFormat":"total","refId":"E"}],"title":"Memory breakdown","type":"timeseries"},{"datasource":{"type":"prometheus","uid":"prometheus"},"description":"Linux Pressure Stall Information: the fraction of time tasks were STALLED waiting for a resource. This is far more honest than a utilisation percentage — memory can read 70% used while processes stall badly on reclaim. Sustained memory PSI above ~0.1 is the precursor to an OOM/eviction event.","fieldConfig":{"defaults":{"custom":{"drawStyle":"line","fillOpacity":20,"lineWidth":1,"showPoints":"never"},"min":0,"thresholds":{"mode":"absolute","steps":[{"color":"green","value":null},{"color":"orange","value":0.1},{"color":"red","value":0.3}]},"unit":"percentunit"},"overrides":[]},"gridPos":{"h":8,"w":12,"x":12,"y":19},"options":{"legend":{"calcs":["mean","max"],"displayMode":"table","placement":"bottom"},"tooltip":{"mode":"multi","sort":"desc"}},"targets":[{"expr":"rate(node_pressure_memory_waiting_seconds_total[5m])","legendFormat":"memory stalled","refId":"A"},{"expr":"rate(node_pressure_cpu_waiting_seconds_total[5m])","legendFormat":"cpu stalled","refId":"B"},{"expr":"rate(node_pressure_io_waiting_seconds_total[5m])","legendFormat":"io stalled","refId":"C"}],"title":"PSI — resource stall (the real 'stress' signal)","type":"timeseries"},{"datasource":{"type":"prometheus","uid":"prometheus"},"description":"Major faults mean the kernel is going to disk to satisfy memory. Under a PHI posture Redis persistence is off, so swap activity here is pure host-level pressure.","fieldConfig":{"defaults":{"custom":{"drawStyle":"line","fillOpacity":10,"lineWidth":1,"showPoints":"never"}},"overrides":[{"matcher":{"id":"byName","options":"swap used"},"properties":[{"id":"unit","value":"bytes"}]}]},"gridPos":{"h":7,"w":12,"x":0,"y":27},"options":{"legend":{"displayMode":"list","placement":"bottom"},"tooltip":{"mode":"multi"}},"targets":[{"expr":"node_memory_SwapTotal_bytes - node_memory_SwapFree_bytes","legendFormat":"swap used","refId":"A"},{"expr":"rate(node_vmstat_pgmajfault[5m])","legendFormat":"major faults/s","refId":"B"}],"title":"Swap \u0026 major page faults","type":"timeseries"},{"datasource":{"type":"prometheus","uid":"prometheus"},"description":"Any non-zero rate is a process being killed for memory. Correlate with the PSI panel.","fieldConfig":{"defaults":{"color":{"fixedColor":"red","mode":"fixed"},"custom":{"drawStyle":"bars","fillOpacity":60,"lineWidth":1,"showPoints":"never"},"min":0,"unit":"short"},"overrides":[]},"gridPos":{"h":7,"w":12,"x":12,"y":27},"options":{"legend":{"displayMode":"list","placement":"bottom"},"tooltip":{"mode":"single"}},"targets":[{"expr":"rate(node_vmstat_oom_kill[5m])","legendFormat":"oom kills/s","refId":"A"}],"title":"OOM kills","type":"timeseries"},{"collapsed":false,"gridPos":{"h":1,"w":24,"x":0,"y":34},"panels":[],"title":"Sockets \u0026 file descriptors","type":"row"},{"datasource":{"type":"prometheus","uid":"prometheus"},"description":"Host-wide socket counts from /proc/net/sockstat. `sockets total` counts socket OBJECTS of every type — TCP, UDP, raw, and the UNIX-domain/netlink sockets held by kubelet, containerd and every pod — and idles near 940 with no HOPE traffic at all. It is NOT a connection count: for live client connections use `TCP established` on the panel to the right, or the gateway's own `hope_api_active_connections_count` on the HOPE — Platform board. A climbing TIME_WAIT with flat in-use means connection churn: a client not pooling. (Corrected 2026-09-18, TASK-989: this text previously credited PgBouncer for keeping the line flat. There is no pooler on this deployment — one in-cluster Postgres, ~12 workloads against max_connections = 200, since TASK-847.)","fieldConfig":{"defaults":{"custom":{"drawStyle":"line","fillOpacity":10,"lineWidth":1,"showPoints":"never"},"min":0,"unit":"short"},"overrides":[]},"gridPos":{"h":8,"w":12,"x":0,"y":35},"options":{"legend":{"calcs":["lastNotNull","max"],"displayMode":"table","placement":"right"},"tooltip":{"mode":"multi","sort":"desc"}},"targets":[{"expr":"node_sockstat_TCP_inuse","legendFormat":"TCP in-use","refId":"A"},{"expr":"node_sockstat_TCP_alloc","legendFormat":"TCP allocated","refId":"B"},{"expr":"node_sockstat_TCP_tw","legendFormat":"TCP TIME_WAIT","refId":"C"},{"expr":"node_sockstat_UDP_inuse","legendFormat":"UDP in-use","refId":"D"},{"expr":"node_sockstat_sockets_used","legendFormat":"sockets total","refId":"E"}],"title":"Open sockets by type","type":"timeseries"},{"datasource":{"type":"prometheus","uid":"prometheus"},"description":"`TCP established` is the real live-connection count for this node. File descriptors are plotted for TREND only: node_filefd_maximum reports LONG_MAX (~9.2e18) here because k3s leaves fs.file-max effectively unlimited, so the dashed ceiling is unreachable and a percent-of-max reading is meaningless. Watch the allocated line's SHAPE — a monotonic climb under flat traffic is a descriptor leak, a step change is a new deployment. (Corrected 2026-09-18, TASK-989; the NodeFileDescriptorsExhausting alert had the same dead ratio and was switched to an absolute threshold.)","fieldConfig":{"defaults":{"custom":{"drawStyle":"line","fillOpacity":10,"lineWidth":1,"showPoints":"never"},"min":0,"unit":"short"},"overrides":[{"matcher":{"id":"byName","options":"fd maximum"},"properties":[{"id":"custom.lineStyle","value":{"dash":[8,6],"fill":"dash"}},{"id":"custom.fillOpacity","value":0},{"id":"color","value":{"fixedColor":"red","mode":"fixed"}}]}]},"gridPos":{"h":8,"w":12,"x":12,"y":35},"options":{"legend":{"calcs":["lastNotNull","max"],"displayMode":"table","placement":"right"},"tooltip":{"mode":"multi","sort":"desc"}},"targets":[{"expr":"node_netstat_Tcp_CurrEstab","legendFormat":"TCP established","refId":"A"},{"expr":"node_filefd_allocated","legendFormat":"file descriptors allocated","refId":"B"},{"expr":"node_filefd_maximum","legendFormat":"fd maximum","refId":"C"}],"title":"Established connections \u0026 file descriptors","type":"timeseries"},{"collapsed":false,"gridPos":{"h":1,"w":24,"x":0,"y":43},"panels":[],"title":"Disk \u0026 network","type":"row"},{"datasource":{"type":"prometheus","uid":"prometheus"},"fieldConfig":{"defaults":{"custom":{"drawStyle":"line","fillOpacity":10,"lineWidth":1,"showPoints":"never"},"unit":"Bps"},"overrides":[]},"gridPos":{"h":8,"w":8,"x":0,"y":44},"options":{"legend":{"displayMode":"list","placement":"bottom"},"tooltip":{"mode":"multi","sort":"desc"}},"targets":[{"expr":"rate(node_disk_read_bytes_total[5m])","legendFormat":"{{device}} read","refId":"A"},{"expr":"rate(node_disk_written_bytes_total[5m])","legendFormat":"{{device}} write","refId":"B"}],"title":"Disk throughput","type":"timeseries"},{"datasource":{"type":"prometheus","uid":"prometheus"},"description":"Fraction of wall-clock the device spent servicing I/O. Sustained near 1 means the disk is the bottleneck.","fieldConfig":{"defaults":{"custom":{"drawStyle":"line","fillOpacity":20,"lineWidth":1,"showPoints":"never"},"min":0,"unit":"percentunit"},"overrides":[]},"gridPos":{"h":8,"w":8,"x":8,"y":44},"options":{"legend":{"displayMode":"list","placement":"bottom"},"tooltip":{"mode":"multi","sort":"desc"}},"targets":[{"expr":"rate(node_disk_io_time_seconds_total[5m])","legendFormat":"{{device}}","refId":"A"}],"title":"Disk busy (io_time)","type":"timeseries"},{"datasource":{"type":"prometheus","uid":"prometheus"},"fieldConfig":{"defaults":{"custom":{"drawStyle":"line","fillOpacity":10,"lineWidth":1,"showPoints":"never"},"unit":"Bps"},"overrides":[]},"gridPos":{"h":8,"w":8,"x":16,"y":44},"options":{"legend":{"displayMode":"list","placement":"bottom"},"tooltip":{"mode":"multi","sort":"desc"}},"targets":[{"expr":"rate(node_network_receive_bytes_total{device!~\"lo|veth.*|cni.*|flannel.*\"}[5m])","legendFormat":"{{device}} rx","refId":"A"},{"expr":"rate(node_network_transmit_bytes_total{device!~\"lo|veth.*|cni.*|flannel.*\"}[5m])","legendFormat":"{{device}} tx","refId":"B"}],"title":"Network throughput","type":"timeseries"}],"refresh":"30s","schemaVersion":39,"tags":["hope","infrastructure","node","task-636"],"templating":{"list":[]},"time":{"from":"now-6h","to":"now"},"timezone":"browser","title":"HOPE — Node \u0026 System Activity","uid":"hope-node-system","version":1}}